    "title": "Elementary Chinese (elementary_chinese_pg13.txt) - 5",
    "content": "1.  Tones \nChinese  is  a  tonal  language.  Tones  are  used  to  differentiate  the \nmeanings between words that have the same syllable. \nThere are four tones in Mandarin Chinese, as shown below: \nWatch  the  following  video  to  learn  how  the  four  tones  are \npronounced: \nOne or more interactive elements has been excluded \nfrom this version of the text. You can view them online \nhere: https://openbooks.lib.msu.edu/chs101/?p=121#oembed-1 \nIn addition, there is a neutral tone, which is pronounced quickly and \nlightly. Syllables with a neutral tone have no tone mark. Watch the \nvideo below to learn how to pronounce it: \nOne or more interactive elements has been excluded \nTones  |  5"
