    "content": "接\njiē\nv., to pick up\n接电话\njiē diàn huà\nv., to take a phone call\n杨\n上\n年级\n用功\n题\n几\nyáng\nshàng\nnián jí\na popular surname in China\nv., to go to\nn., grade\nyòng gōng\nadj., hard-working, diligent\ntí\njī\nn., question/problem items; title, topic\nadj., several, a few, a couple of\n怎么了\nzěn me le\nquestion word, used to ask “what’s happened”,\n“what’s the matter”\n练习\nliàn xí\nv./n., to practice/exercise\n办公室\nbàn gōng shì\nn., office\n开会\nkāi huì\nv., to have a meeting\n就\njiù\nadv., as early as\nadv., used before verbs or prepositional\nphrases to indicate emphasis\n但是\n得\n见面\n行\n上班\n下班\n下课\n方便\n空\ndàn shì\nconj., but\nděi\nmodal verb, have to/must\njiàn miàn\nv., to meet\nxíng\nadj., alright/okay\nshàng bān\nv., to go to work, to work\nxià bān\nv., to finish work\nxià kè\nv., to finish classes\nfāng biàn\nadj., convenient\nkòng\nn., availability, free time\n星巴克\nxīng bā kè\n挂\nguà\nv., to hang\n118  |  Lesson 6 Dialogue 2: Calling a Friend"
